      },
      "message": "fix(contour): enter every bore-side ring by the stated entry\n\nA bore-side contour with several rings entered only the first ring by its\nramp or helix. Each later ring at the same level went through the pass\nlink, which lifted and plunged straight into solid with no note. A ring\nafter another one now takes the entry on its first level and the level\ntransition below it. The pass link still feeds straight where the\nkeep-down proof holds.\n\nFixes #3830\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
